10. ROUND-3 review of 7cc4c7a5 (scratchpad/review-k058-r3.md): 3 LOW, all addressed.

    LOW 1 — the outer join re-opens a debtors-vs-aging disagreement in the
    OPPOSITE direction: arAgingService.ts:49 still joins customers with an
    unscoped INNER JOIN, so an id matching no customers row anywhere is now
    listed by the debtors dashboard and still dropped by aging.
    DOCUMENTED, NOT ALIGNED — and asserted, which the review offered as the
    alternative. Reason for not aligning: arAgingService.ts is K-053's
    affectedPath in docs/audits/remediation/backlog.json
    ("src/modules/accounting/services/ar/arAgingService.ts:53") and two K-053
    fixers are editing it on parallel branches right now. Editing the same
    statement from K-058's branch would conflict at integration and take another
    item's scope. Recorded in fix.md Limits AND pinned by a new test so a future
    change to either surface fails rather than drifting silently.

    LOW 2 — "the debtors summary agrees with AR aging" never called getARAging;
    it compared a sum against a hardcoded constant. FIXED: the test now calls
    getARAging(COMPANY), sums the buckets and compares the two surfaces, then
    keeps the constant as a second assertion so a change that moves BOTH
    surfaces together is still caught.

    LOW 3 — two different un-nameable debtors both rendered "Unknown customer",
    indistinguishable in the table and in the dashboard's clientName search
    (pages/accounting/debtors-manager/index.tsx:143). FIXED as suggested:
    COALESCE(c.name, 'Unknown customer ' || left(COALESCE(ci.client_id,
    ci.customer_id)::text, 8)) on both projections. The inner COALESCE is the
    summary's own grouping expression, so GROUP BY is unaffected.

